  "question": {
    "text": "The area of the region (in sq. units), in the first quadrant bounded by the parabola $y=9 x^2$ and the lines $x=0, y=1$ and $y=4$, is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "msQvY",
      "text": "\n$7 / 9$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FK9eD",
      "text": "\n$14 / 3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7HrYW",
      "text": "\n$7 / 3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9YVUC",
      "text": "\n$14 / 9$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { Required area }=\\int_{y=1}^4 \\sqrt{\\frac{y}{9}} d y \\\\\n& =\\frac{1}{3} \\int_{y=1}^4 y^{1 / 2} d y=\\frac{1}{3} \\times\\left.\\frac{2}{3}\\left(y^{3 / 2}\\right)\\right|_1 ^4 \\\\\n& =\\frac{2}{9}\\left[\\left(4^{1 / 2}\\right)^3-\\left(1^{1 / 2}\\right)^3\\right]=\\frac{2}{9}[8-1]\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n=\\frac{2}{9} \\times 7=\\frac{14}{9} \\text { sq. units. }\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
